to shriek
KJV: cry, groan.

H603.definition:
from H602 (אָנַק);
shrieking
KJV: crying out, groaning, sighing.

H604.definition:
the same as H603 (אֲנָקָה);
some kind of lizard, probably the gecko (from its wail)
KJV: ferret.

H605.definition:
a primitive root;
to be frail, feeble, or (figuratively) melancholy
KJV: desperate(-ly wicked), incurable, sick, woeful.

H606.definition:
(Aramaic) or אֱנַשׁ; (Aramaic), corresponding to H582 (אֱנוֹשׁ);
a man
KJV: man, [phrase] whosoever.

H607.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H859 (אַתָּה);
thou
KJV: as for thee, thou.

H608.definition:
(Aramaic) plural of H607 (אַנְתָּה);
ye
KJV: ye.

H609.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
