KJV: Asenath.

H622.definition:
a primitive root;
to gather for any purpose; hence, to receive, take away, i.e. remove (destroy, leave behind, put up, restore, etc.)
KJV: assemble, bring, consume, destroy, felch, gather (in, together, up again), [idiom] generally, get (him), lose, put all together, receive, recover (another from leprosy), (be) rereward, [idiom] surely, take (away, into, up), [idiom] utterly, withdraw.

H623.definition:
from H622 (אָסַף); collector;
Asaph, the name of three Israelites, and of the family of the first
KJV: Asaph.

H624.definition:
passive participle of H622 (אָסַף);
collected (only in the plural), i.e. a collection of offerings)
KJV: threshold, Asuppim.

H625.definition:
from H622 (אָסַף);
a collection (of fruits)
KJV: gathering.

H626.definition:
from H622 (אָסַף);
a collection of people (only adverbial)
KJV: [idiom] together.

H627.definition:
feminine of H624 (אָסֻף);
a collection of (learned) men (only in the plural)
KJV: assembly.

H628.definition:
by reduplication from H624 (אָסֻף);
gathered up together, i.e. a promiscuous assemblage (of people)
KJV: mixt multitude.

H629.definition:
