to yoke or hitch; by analogy, to fasten in any sense, to join battle
KJV: bind, fast, gird, harness, hold, keep, make ready, order, prepare, prison(-er), put in bonds, set in array, tie.

H632.definition:
or אִסָּר; from H631 (אָסַר);
