properly, the nose or nostril; hence, the face, and occasionally a person; also (from the rapid breathing in passion) ire
KJV: anger(-gry), [phrase] before, countenance, face, [phrase] forebearing, forehead, [phrase] (long-) suffering, nose, nostril, snout, [idiom] worthy, wrath.

H640.definition:
a primitive root (rather a denominative from H646 (אֵפוֹד));
to gird on (the ephod)
KJV: bind, gird.

H641.definition:
the same as H646 (אֵפוֹד) shortened;
Ephod, an Israelite
KJV: Ephod.

H642.definition:
feminine of H646 (אֵפוֹד);
a girding on (of the ephod); hence, generally, a plating (of metal)
KJV: ephod, ornament.

H643.definition:
apparently of foreign derivation;
